To create a TabView in SwiftUI with multiple full-screen vertical scroll views that can be swiped like pages, follow these steps:



1. Import the SwiftUI framework in your Swift file.



```swift
import SwiftUI
```

2. Create a struct that conforms to the View protocol, where you'll design the user interface.

```swift
struct ContentView: View {
    var body: some View {
        // Your code will go here
    }
}
```

3. Create a TabView, and use the .tabViewStyle(PageTabViewStyle()) modifier to enable swiping between tabs like pages.

```swift
TabView {
    // Your ScrollViews will go here
}
.tabViewStyle(PageTabViewStyle())
.edgesIgnoringSafeArea(.all) // Makes the contents full screen
.animation(.default)
```

4. Add multiple vertical scroll views inside the TabView. For example, we'll add three scroll views with different colored backgrounds.

```swift
ScrollView(.vertical, showsIndicators: false) {
    VStack {
        Text("Page 1")
        Spacer()
    }
    .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)
    .background(Color.red)
}
ScrollView(.vertical, showsIndicators: false) {
    VStack {
        Text("Page 2")
        Spacer()
    }
    .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)
    .background(Color.green)
}
ScrollView(.vertical, showsIndicators: false) {
    VStack {
        Text("Page 3")
        Spacer()
    }
    .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)
    .background(Color.blue)
}
```

Now, put everything together:

```swift
import SwiftUI

struct ContentView: View {
    var body: some View {
        TabView {
            ScrollView(.vertical, showsIndicators: false) {
                VStack {
                    Text("Page 1")
                    Spacer()
                }
                .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)
                .background(Color.red)
            }
            ScrollView(.vertical, showsIndicators: false) {
                VStack {
                    Text("Page 2")
                    Spacer()
                }
                .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)
                .background(Color.green)
            }
            ScrollView(.vertical, showsIndicators: false) {
                VStack {
                    Text("Page 3")
                    Spacer()
                }
                .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity)
                .background(Color.blue)
            }
        }
        .tabViewStyle(PageTabViewStyle())
        .edgesIgnoringSafeArea(.all)
        .animation(.default)
    }
}

struct ContentView_Previews: PreviewProvider {
    static var previews: some View {
        ContentView()
    }
}
```

The ContentView now contains a TabView with three full-screen vertical scroll views. You can swipe horizontally between these scrollviews to switch pages.
